WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.944 --> 00:00:18.788
Daisy have much time.

2
00:00:18.808 --> 00:00:23.089
"Tosca, what should I tell adopters?

3
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.530
Is there anything unusual about you?"

4
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.011
"You mean besides my beautiful voice?"

5
00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:30.331
Tosca asked.

6
00:00:32.844 --> 00:00:34.585
"Hmm. I can walk on a leash.

7
00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:38.767
Antonio and I went on lovely walks together."

8
00:00:39.947 --> 00:00:41.047
Daisy was excited.

9
00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:44.089
"Lots of people would love to walk with their cats!"

10
00:00:45.349 --> 00:00:46.610
She grabbed Kaleem's arm.

11
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.010
"Let's go!"

12
00:00:53.873 --> 00:00:57.234
Soon they spotted a couple with a baby sleeping in a stroller.

13
00:00:57.854 --> 00:01:01.376
Daisy told them about the pretty Siamese who walked on a leash.

14
00:01:02.852 --> 00:01:06.435
"It would be fun to walk that cat with our baby," the dad said.

15
00:01:06.455 --> 00:01:07.916
"Follow me!"

16
00:01:14.261 --> 00:01:15.863
Daisy led them to the tent.

17
00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:19.125
"What a beautiful cat!"

18
00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:20.166
the mom said.

19
00:01:20.186 --> 00:01:23.869
"It's nice to be appreciated."

20
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.491
Tosca's eyes went wide.

21
00:01:26.511 --> 00:01:32.356
"Yooowl!" The baby woke up and started to wail.

22
00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.661
"Let's get out of here!"

23
00:01:34.941 --> 00:01:35.721
the dad said.

24
00:01:35.741 --> 00:01:36.961
"Sorry, kids.

25
00:01:37.622 --> 00:01:39.783
We can't have a cat that wakes the baby."

26
00:01:41.063 --> 00:01:42.043
Daisy sighed.

27
00:01:43.764 --> 00:01:46.225
Then she noticed Kaleem bopping his head again.

28
00:01:46.245 --> 00:01:49.707
"How can you hear the band above all this racket?"

29
00:01:50.447 --> 00:01:51.207
Kaleem shrugged.

30
00:01:51.227 --> 00:01:53.008
"I like music?"

31
00:01:54.428 --> 00:01:55.869
"Oh," Daisy said.

32
00:01:56.569 --> 00:01:57.470
Then she gasped.

33
00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:02.732
"Wait! I think Tosca first started yowling when the band started playing.

34
00:02:03.988 --> 00:02:05.829
Are you afraid of music, Tosca?"

35
00:02:06.289 --> 00:02:09.270
Tosca was so surprised that she stopped yowling.

36
00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:13.332
"No. I love music!

37
00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:15.793
Antonio was an opera singer.

38
00:02:15.813 --> 00:02:18.935
He even named me after an opera."

39
00:02:19.855 --> 00:02:22.976
She returned to yowling as Joan hurried over.

40
00:02:22.997 --> 00:02:24.777
"I found a driver."

41
00:02:24.797 --> 00:02:28.799
"Please don't send Tosca away yet," Daisy said.

42
00:02:28.819 --> 00:02:30.600
"I have an idea!"

43
00:02:37.428 --> 00:02:40.169
Daisy took off for the bandstand.

44
00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:41.890
Riley was finishing a song.

45
00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:45.531
When he stopped singing, the yowling stopped too.

46
00:02:45.551 --> 00:02:49.432
"I was right," Daisy thought.

47
00:02:50.072 --> 00:02:52.052
"Riley! I found your new muse!"

48
00:02:53.213 --> 00:02:53.773
He grinned.

49
00:02:53.793 --> 00:02:55.693
"You found me a new parrot?"

50
00:02:57.474 --> 00:02:59.314
"Not exactly," Daisy said.

51
00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:03.115
"Your wife isn't afraid of cats, is she?"

52
00:03:03.135 --> 00:03:07.490
"No. She loves them—she's even been talking about adopting one."

53
00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.932
"Quick! Come with me!"

54
00:03:10.272 --> 00:03:10.893
Daisy said.

55
00:03:14.035 --> 00:03:16.838
Inside the cat tent, Riley scratched his head.

56
00:03:16.858 --> 00:03:18.699
"Tosca is pretty.

57
00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:20.881
But she's a short-haired cat.

58
00:03:22.423 --> 00:03:24.324
My wife always had long-haired cats."

59
00:03:26.446 --> 00:03:29.909
"Well, this is a very special cat," Daisy said.

60
00:03:29.929 --> 00:03:31.550
"She wasn't yowling.

61
00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:33.232
She was singing!

62
00:03:34.164 --> 00:03:36.026
Her first owner was an opera singer.

63
00:03:36.606 --> 00:03:38.027
She used to sing along with him.

64
00:03:38.748 --> 00:03:40.830
And today she's been singing along with you!"

65
00:03:42.211 --> 00:03:43.352
Joan looked uncertain.

66
00:03:43.372 --> 00:03:45.974
"Sing something, Riley."

67
00:03:45.994 --> 00:03:48.896
"Um, okay."

68
00:03:50.077 --> 00:03:55.261
Riley hesitated, then sang, "La, la, la!"

69
00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.944
Tosca immediately started yowling.

70
00:03:59.985 --> 00:04:02.948
Joan groaned as all the dogs started barking again.

71
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.621
But Riley's face lit up.

72
00:04:05.641 --> 00:04:07.362
"A singing cat?

73
00:04:07.882 --> 00:04:08.602
She's perfect!

74
00:04:09.142 --> 00:04:09.743
I'll take her!"

75
00:04:14.845 --> 00:04:18.166
A few days later, Daisy and Kaleem were at recess.

76
00:04:19.747 --> 00:04:21.648
Beatrice sat on Daisy's headband.

77
00:04:22.688 --> 00:04:23.628
Grace ran over.

78
00:04:23.648 --> 00:04:27.170
"I had a clarinet lesson yesterday.

79
00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.831
Riley loves Tosca!"

80
00:04:29.851 --> 00:04:32.032
"Great!" Kaleem said.

81
00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:33.933
Grace nodded.

82
00:04:33.953 --> 00:04:36.194
"His wife takes her for long walks.

83
00:04:37.035 --> 00:04:39.096
And Tosca goes to the band's rehearsals.

84
00:04:39.777 --> 00:04:42.459
She even inspired Riley to write a new song!"

85
00:04:48.303 --> 00:04:51.125
As Grace left, Beatrice buzzed loudly.

86
00:04:51.145 --> 00:04:53.306
"Another success!

87
00:04:54.007 --> 00:04:55.427
I told them you could do it."

88
00:04:55.448 --> 00:04:58.089
"What?" Daisy froze.

89
00:04:58.109 --> 00:04:59.410
"Told who?"

90
00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:05.965
"Oops! Er, I just realized it's springtime," Beatrice said.

91
00:05:05.985 --> 00:05:07.931
"I've got some plants to pollinate.

92
00:05:08.653 --> 00:05:09.054
Bye!"
